  "lesson": {
    "kind": "deepen",
    "focusPoint": 3,
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Choosing the right tense",
        "body": "Practice simple vs compound decisions. (1) finished yesterday → simple past; (2) experience up to now → present perfect; (3) past habit → imperfect/used to; (4) present hypothesis → conditional; (5) already done before another past → pluperfect.\n\nRewrite five short sentences changing only the tense and explain what nuance shifts. The goal is to hear aspect and time-anchor differences, not only memorize labels.\n\nSelf-check: can you justify each choice in one sentence? If not, return to finished / have finished / had finished."
      }
    ],
